kim kardashian and kanye west reunite to  pay their respects to the late virgil  ablo at his final louis vuitton show in  miami  kim may have filed for divorce from the  grammy winner back in february but on  tuesday the two came together for a  special occasion a showing of the former  artistic director's spring summer 2022  collection marking his final  presentation the exes posed for this  pick with their eight-year-old daughter  north and the kkw beauty founder shared  several moments from the night on her  insta story including a giant hot air  balloon with the louis vuitton logo a  statue of virgil a fireworks show and a  drone choreographed light show with an  animated paper plane before revealing  the words virgil was here in the sky and  i love that the off-white founder and  artistic director for louis vuitton died  over the weekend following a private  two-year battle with cancer he was 41  years old following news of his passing  stars like drake haley bieber gigi hadid  kendall jenner tracy ellis ross idris  elba pharrell and more share their  condolences on social media kim posted  several pics with virgil to instagram  writing in part quote this one is hard  to process i can't even believe i am  writing this we will miss you so much  virgil and love you so much  but kim and kanye weren't the only stars  in attendance at tuesday's event maluma  ricky martin 21 savage lil baby gunna  and metro boomin were there while cuevo  kid cudi and offset modeled in the  runway show  [Music]  [Laughter]  and in a post to louis vuitton's  instagram page michael burke the  chairman and ceo explained it was the  designer's wish for the show to go on  quote virgil was not only a friend great  collaborator creative genius visionary  and disruptor but also one of the best  cultural communicators of our time he  paved the way for future generations  michael added that virgil was a quote  eternal optimist who believed anything  was possible in this same spirit we at  louis vuitton will proudly continue to  celebrate his legacy with a final show  in miami her his wishes  [Music]  and in a live stream the show closed out  by sharing some sweet words from virgil  himself there's no limit  life is so short  that  you can't waste even a day  subscribing to what someone thinks you  can do versus knowing what you can do  you
 

